-- Every estimated number carries the word **estimate** in the same line or the sentence directly
-  under it (`Estimated in body · a model, not a blood level`).
-- The source/method is **one tap away** from any estimate (a `Source` or `How this is
-  calculated` row). Never removed to save space.
-- Visual rule: estimates are drawn as a line in `data` blue; measured values the user entered
-  (weigh-ins, labs) are drawn as **points**. Projections are dashed. The eye can always tell a
-  model from a measurement.
-- The design never shows a recommendation, a "good/bad" verdict color on a health value, or a
-  suggested dose change. Color states describe *schedule and supply*, not the body.
