 ## 8. Empty-state rule
 
 An empty screen shows **one question and one action**. Nothing else competes.
 
-- Never render a disabled primary button, a `-`/`—` placeholder, `0 of N`, `Nothing yet`, or an
-  empty chart as a state the user must read.
-- A feature whose prerequisite is missing does **not** render; at most one `Next:` line says
-  what it unlocks after the current step.
-- Explanatory copy in an empty state: max one sentence.
-- The empty state uses the same raised object as the filled state (same place, same size
-  class), so the screen does not jump when data arrives.
+- Never a disabled primary button, `-`/`—`, `0 of N`, `Nothing yet`, or an empty chart.
+- A feature whose prerequisite is missing does not render; at most one `Next:` line.
+- Max one sentence of explanation.
+- The empty state uses the same raised object in the same place as the filled state.
 
